        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): bound model run image reads with per-file and aggregate budget",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `readModelRunImageFiles` function in `src/cli/capability-cli/model.ts` reads image files for model run capability. It used a TOCTOU-prone pattern: `statSync(path)` to check file size (100 MiB per-file cap + 500 MiB aggregate budget), then a separate `fs.readFile(path)` to read the content. Between the stat and the read, the file could be swapped with a much larger one, defeating the size cap.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nModel run files are user-supplied inputs that could be symlink-swapped or replaced between the stat validation and the read. While the per-file and aggregate budgets provide defense-in-depth, the TOCTOU window means an attacker who can control the file at the path can bypass the per-file cap. Opening the file first and operating on the same descriptor eliminates this race.\n\n## What Changed\n\nReplaced the path-based `statSync` + `await fs.readFile` pattern with descriptor-bound reads using `fs.promises.open`:\n\n```typescript\nconst handle = await fs.open(resolvedPath, \"r\");\ntry {\n  const stat = await handle.stat();\n  if (!stat.isFile()) throw new Error(\"not a regular file\");\n  if (stat.size > MAX_MODEL_RUN_IMAGE_BYTES) throw new Error(\"file too large\");\n  budget.remaining -= stat.size;\n  return await handle.readFile();\n} finally {\n  await handle.close();\n}\n```\n\nKey points:\n- `fs.promises.open()` returns a `FileHandle` — `stat()` and `readFile()` both operate on the same descriptor\n- `try/finally` guarantees `handle.close()` even when exceptions are thrown\n- Per-file 100 MiB cap and 500 MiB aggregate budget are preserved from the original implementation\n- `import { statSync }` was removed as no longer needed\n- Sequential processing (already in original) is retained\n\n## User Impact\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| `statSync(path)` → TOCTOU race: file could be swapped before read | → fd pins the inode; race impossible |\n| Normal model run with valid files → works | → works (unchanged) |\n| Per-file 100 MiB cap + 500 MiB aggregate budget | → preserved, now without TOCTOU |\n\n## Evidence\n\n**All 109 capability-cli tests pass:**\n\n```\n ✓ |cli| src/cli/capability-cli.test.ts (109 tests) 3133ms\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  109 passed (109)\n```\n\nThe descriptor-bound pattern is the standard fix for TOCTOU file races — the fd pins the specific inode, preventing substitution between validation and consumption.\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\nRan the production `openclaw --dev capability model run --local` command against real image files using the branch build. Paths redacted to `<tmp>`.\n\n### Accepted image (within 100 MiB per-file cap)\n\n```\n$ openclaw --dev capability model run --prompt \"hello\" --file <tmp>/tiny.png --local --json\n```\n\nRelevant JSON excerpt:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"capability\": \"model.run\",\n  \"transport\": \"local\",\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"<tmp>/tiny.png\",\n      \"mimeType\": \"image/png\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Hello! I see that you've mentioned an image...\",\n      \"mediaUrl\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe 70-byte PNG is accepted, loaded via the descriptor-bound path, and passed to the model as an `image/png` input.\n\n### Per-file rejection (>100 MiB)\n\n```\n$ openclaw --dev capability model run --prompt \"hello\" --file <tmp>/huge.png --local --json\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\nError: --file too large: <tmp>/huge.png is 110100480 bytes (max 104857600)\n```\n\nThe 105 MiB file is rejected before any read, because the size check is performed on the same opened file descriptor that would be used for `readFile`.\n\n### Aggregate-budget rejection (>500 MiB total)\n\n```\n$ openclaw --dev capability model run --prompt \"hello\" \\\n  --file <tmp>/medium1.png --file <tmp>/medium2.png --file <tmp>/medium3.png \\\n  --file <tmp>/medium4.png --file <tmp>/medium5.png --file <tmp>/medium6.png \\\n  --local --json\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\nError: --file too large: <tmp>/medium6.png is 94371840 bytes (max remaining total budget 52428800)\n```\n\nSix 90 MiB images total 540 MiB. The first five consume 450 MiB of the 500 MiB aggregate budget; the sixth is rejected because it exceeds the remaining 50 MiB, proving the aggregate cap is enforced across the invocation.",
        "branch": "fix/bound-model-run-files",
